WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.333
What if an animal

2
00:00:01.333 --> 00:00:02.000
could reverse

3
00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:03.367
its own life cycle?

4
00:00:03.533 --> 00:00:04.667
This is

5
00:00:04.667 --> 00:00:05.800
Turritopsis dohrnii.

6
00:00:05.967 --> 00:00:07.367
Normally, attached polyps

7
00:00:07.367 --> 00:00:09.233
bud off tiny jellyfish,

8
00:00:09.233 --> 00:00:10.633
which grow into

9
00:00:10.633 --> 00:00:11.567
swimming adults.

10
00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:13.500
But injury or starvation

11
00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:15.167
can send an adult

12
00:00:15.167 --> 00:00:16.033
another way.

13
00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:17.633
Its bell collapses.

14
00:00:17.633 --> 00:00:19.067
Its tentacles disappear.

15
00:00:19.067 --> 00:00:20.500
It settles into

16
00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:21.967
a cyst-like mass.

17
00:00:22.167 --> 00:00:24.200
Inside, cells reorganize.

18
00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:26.200
Some can change

19
00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:28.233
their specialized identity:

20
00:00:28.233 --> 00:00:28.900
transdifferentiation.

21
00:00:29.133 --> 00:00:30.433
A stolon grows,

22
00:00:30.433 --> 00:00:31.300
then polyps.

23
00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:33.033
That colony can bud

24
00:00:33.033 --> 00:00:33.900
new jellyfish.

25
00:00:34.233 --> 00:00:35.467
Life-cycle reversal

26
00:00:35.467 --> 00:00:37.300
can happen repeatedly

27
00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:39.133
in laboratory cultures.

28
00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:40.600
The molecular controls

29
00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:42.300
are still being studied.

30
00:00:42.467 --> 00:00:43.400
But predators

31
00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:45.233
can still kill it.

32
00:00:45.233 --> 00:00:46.167
Reversal isn't

33
00:00:46.167 --> 00:00:47.100
guaranteed survival.

34
00:00:47.333 --> 00:00:48.667
It doesn't make

35
00:00:48.667 --> 00:00:49.567
death impossible.

36
00:00:49.567 --> 00:00:51.367
It makes the direction

37
00:00:51.367 --> 00:00:52.700
of development reversible.
